  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Task B: one-pair family on W1\n<0|t(theta_2) = lambda <0|rho_2(G) (site 2 only). Then 1 + a t(theta_2) gives rho_2(1 - kappa G) with a = -kappa/lambda. Compute lambda for n=2,4,6 sites at several theta points; test against products of theta differences.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "bkLamData[n_, th_List] := Module[{vac, t, psi, vecs, tgt, lam, res},\n vecs = bkVecs[bkW1, n]; vac = Flatten[KroneckerProduct @@ vecs];\n t = bkTrans[n, N[th[[1 ;; n]]], bkGzN, N[th[[2]]]];\n psi = vac . t; vecs[[2]] = vecs[[2]] . bkGzN; tgt = Flatten[KroneckerProduct @@ vecs];\n lam = (psi . tgt)/(tgt . tgt); res = Norm[psi - lam tgt]/Norm[psi]; {lam, res}];\nbkThPts = {bkthAll, {1/3, -1/4, 5/7, -2/9, 3/11, -5/6}, {-1/5, 2/3, 1/9, 3/4, -7/8, 1/6}};\nbkLamTab = Table[Join[{n, p}, bkLamData[n, bkThPts[[p]]]], {n, {2, 4, 6}}, {p, 3}] // Flatten[#, 1] &;\nGrid[Prepend[bkLamTab, {\"n\", \"theta pt\", \"lambda\", \"rel resid\"}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
