  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task E (redo, continued): eigenstates with non-zero overlap with <0|\nThe Krylov space of <0| under t(u0) has dimension > 300 (stopped at 300 with residual 0.24), so many eigenstates overlap. Left Ritz vectors phi = y.Q of the Krylov matrix; keep converged ones (|phi t - tau phi| small), then obtain the matching RIGHT eigenvectors Psi by inverse iteration on t(u0). Check Psi is an eigenvector of t at u = -0.77, theta2, theta4; then test <X|Psi> = P(tau2,tau4) <0|Psi> for B (kappa=0.5) and C (kappa=0.5) bras and also for the three-pair target of D (P built from the free-coefficient LSQ fit).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "bkRitz = Eigensystem[Transpose[bkTK]];\nbkPhis = Table[bkRitz[[2, j]] . bkQK, {j, Length[bkRitz[[1]]]}];\nbkRitzRes = Table[Norm[bkPhis[[j]] . bkT0 - bkRitz[[1, j]] bkPhis[[j]]]/Norm[bkRitz[[1, j]] bkPhis[[j]]], {j, Length[bkPhis]}];\nbkConv = Select[Ordering[bkRitzRes], bkRitzRes[[#]] < 10^-8 &];\nbkConv5 = Take[SortBy[bkConv, -Abs[bkRitz[[1, #]]] &], UpTo[5]];\nbkRight[tau_] := Module[{x = RandomComplex[{-1 - I, 1 + I}, 4096], A = bkT0 - (tau + 10^-6) IdentityMatrix[4096, SparseArray], lu}, lu = LinearSolve[A]; Do[x = lu[x]; x = x/Norm[x], {3}]; x];\nSeedRandom[7]; bkPsis = Table[bkRight[bkRitz[[1, j]]], {j, bkConv5}];\nbkRowsE1b = Table[{j, bkRitz[[1, bkConv5[[i]]]], bkRitzRes[[bkConv5[[i]]]], bkResE[bkT0, bkPsis[[i]]], bkResE[bkTsel[\"u=-0.77\"], bkPsis[[i]]], bkResE[bkTsel[\"th2\"], bkPsis[[i]]], bkResE[bkTsel[\"th4\"], bkPsis[[i]]], Abs[bkVac6 . bkPsis[[i]]]/(Norm[bkVac6] Norm[bkPsis[[i]]])}, {i, Length[bkConv5]}] /. j -> i;\nbkShow[\"E_eig2\", Join[{{\"#converged left Ritz (res<1e-8)\", Length[bkConv], \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"}, {\"state\", \"tau(u0)\", \"left Ritz res\", \"right res u0\", \"res u=-0.77\", \"res th2\", \"res th4\", \"|<0|Psi>|/norms\"}}, bkRowsE1b]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<details class=\"vscode-wolfram-message-output\" style=\"color:#f44;border-left:3px solid #f44;background:rgba(255,68,68,0.08);padding:2px 6px;margin:1px 0;border-radius:0 3px 3px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:0.85em\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer\">4 warnings</summary><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">LinearSolve::luc: Result for LinearSolve of badly conditioned matrix SparseArray[&lt;1818244&gt;, {4096, 4096}] may contain significant numerical errors.</div><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">LinearSolve::luc: Result for LinearSolve of badly conditioned matrix SparseArray[&lt;1818244&gt;, {4096, 4096}] may contain significant numerical errors.</div><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">LinearSolve::luc: Result for LinearSolve of badly conditioned matrix SparseArray[&lt;1818244&gt;, {4096, 4096}] may contain significant numerical errors.</div><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">General::stop: Further output of LinearSolve::luc will be suppressed during this calculation.</div></details>",
